                        "form": "die Rhizome"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1f850679-d6bd-38b8-ab93-8703b5ae7121",
                        "entry_id": "f28683cc-6da4-3aac-9f66-60934737378a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "nährstoffspeichernder, einer Wurzel ähnelnder Teil des Sprosses vieler Stauden in (oder knapp in) der Erde senkrecht oder waagrecht wachsend"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f46f24cd-59df-45ab-89b9-37ca598cb756",
                                "sense_id": "1f850679-d6bd-38b8-ab93-8703b5ae7121",
                                "text": "Die Schwertlilie hat fleischige Rhizome."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6612dc0-0768-4090-96fb-206333c41640",
                                "sense_id": "1f850679-d6bd-38b8-ab93-8703b5ae7121",
                                "text": "Ein Rhizom ist ein verzweigtes Sprossachsensystem, wie es Gartenbesitzer bei Unkräutern wie dem Giersch fürchten."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a73bf26e-e31e-47cf-b375-cd4cf5652e8b",
                                "sense_id": "1f850679-d6bd-38b8-ab93-8703b5ae7121",
                                "text": "Rößler vermutet, dass sich die Schachtelhalme über ein Rhizom vermehrten, von dem aber bei der ausgewachsenen Pflanze nichts übrig blieb."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "93dfc4cc-0772-4c30-a28b-5b95e2ea0fda",
                                "sense_id": "1f850679-d6bd-38b8-ab93-8703b5ae7121",
                                "text": "„Liegt das Rhizom waagrecht im Boden, so streckt es sich und schiebt seine Endknospe vorwärts.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6eefb44f-af8e-4e0c-8e2b-7892fdadd152",
                        "source_entry_id": "f28683cc-6da4-3aac-9f66-60934737378a",
                        "source_sense_id": "1f850679-d6bd-38b8-ab93-8703b5ae7121",
                        "target_lang_word": "rhizome",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rhizome",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a78c26c-097e-3664-a972-9a7f0f03247c",
                                        "entry_id": "7572c79f-46f2-3707-8785-7a10c573e6c9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A horizontal, underground stem of some plants that sends out roots and shoots (scions) from its nodes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "271affda-b259-40ec-9e9d-12a62f2bc3f5",
                                                "sense_id": "1a78c26c-097e-3664-a972-9a7f0f03247c",
                                                "text": "All these species are climbing, briery plants, having long slender roots, which proceed in all directions from a common rootstalk or rhizome."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08698ad9-bab0-3d7c-8ab8-5ac1feec8368",
                                        "entry_id": "7572c79f-46f2-3707-8785-7a10c573e6c9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A so-called “image of thought” that apprehends multiplicities."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a8822b3-785c-4197-89a5-f98c9ffb7fab",
                                                "sense_id": "08698ad9-bab0-3d7c-8ab8-5ac1feec8368",
                                                "text": "The corpus of Kafka's writing, they argue, is ‘a rhizome, a burrow’ (K 7)—an uncentered and meandering growth like crab grass, a complex, aleatory network of pathways like a rabbit warren. A rhizome, as Deleuze and Guattari explain in Rhizome: an Introduction (1976), is the antithesis of a root-tree structure, or ‘arborescence’, the structural model which has dominated Western thought from Porphyrian trees, to Linnaean taxonomies, to Chomskyan sentence diagrams."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "193b2fa5-43e2-4734-925f-07e9c417899e",
                                                "sense_id": "08698ad9-bab0-3d7c-8ab8-5ac1feec8368",
                                                "text": "Critical theorists have often drawn from Deleuze and Guattari's notion of the rhizome when discussing the potential of the Internet. While the Internet may structurally appear as a rhizome, its day-to-day usage by millions via search engines precludes experiencing the random interconnectedness and potential democratizing function."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ef7a6033-0b76-4b21-bfe6-dbf4df0d20eb",
                        "source_entry_id": "f28683cc-6da4-3aac-9f66-60934737378a",
                        "source_sense_id": "1f850679-d6bd-38b8-ab93-8703b5ae7121",
                        "target_lang_word": "rhizome",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rhizome",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "466fefcc-d8fe-3402-8eac-644ba72df193",
                                        "entry_id": "d63db44f-58df-3138-b5b8-8874a26b08fd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tige souterraine, généralement horizontale, de certaines plantes vivaces."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "247aa6aa-e7b5-46cc-962e-b1c089007ee1",
                                                "sense_id": "466fefcc-d8fe-3402-8eac-644ba72df193",
                                                "text": "Divisez les plantes bulbeuses et les vivaces à rhizome"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d94b7e9-2e5b-4bed-866a-46812a33a01b",
                                                "sense_id": "466fefcc-d8fe-3402-8eac-644ba72df193",
                                                "text": "Comment expliquer les effets toxiques constatés sur le rhizome après les applications foliaires d’amitrole ?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3889170b-a754-491f-868f-63123ccf7747",
                                                "sense_id": "466fefcc-d8fe-3402-8eac-644ba72df193",
                                                "text": "En Afrique et dans le Pacifique du Sud, la cochenille Aspidiella hardii est un insecte suceur qui infeste les rhizomes encore au champ […] Les rhizomes infestés finissent par se dessécher. On parvient à lutter contre ce phénomène en plongeant les rhizomes de semence dans du phosalone, du monocrotophos ou du quinalphos."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "108ea90b-1c32-4bf3-8141-231c481d27bb",
                                                "sense_id": "466fefcc-d8fe-3402-8eac-644ba72df193",
                                                "text": "ta langue s’active traverse le tronc\nde ton corps se rend aux racines\naux origines – déjoue les rhizomes\nintuables – des pistils de fleurs\nt’éclairent créent un éblouissement\nfou dans tes yeux"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
